WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.010
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.900
<b>Noukin</b>

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.900
<b>Souwa</b>

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.230
They managed to close 
the gap to eight points.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.780
It's hard to tell which 
way this game will go.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.670
Change courts! Souwa raiding!

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.780
The game will resume with the second half!

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.380
Watch yourself, Takaya.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.750
Will do.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.000
<i>Things are simple from here on out.</i>

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.630
<i>We attack each other and 
the strongest beast wins.</i>

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.790
<i>I'm going to sink you, Ojo-san.</i>

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.550
Kabaddi.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.240
If you see an opening, go for a catch!

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:58.970
Yeah.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.420
Kabaddi... Kabaddi!

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.370
<i>Well, I guess I wouldn't be able 
to touch him with a frontal attack.</i>

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.890
<i>And this guy, more than being super-fast,</i>

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.750
<i>seems like he can totally read all 
my moves and counters in advance.</i>

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:18.530
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:15.990
<i>If there's one advantage I have over 
Ojo-san, it's probably that I'm stronger.</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.530
<i>Should I let him catch me and shake him off?</i>

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.530
<i>Come on. Here's some bait.</i>

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:27.120
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.580
<i>He's not coming? Maybe he's being wary.</i>

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.980
<i>Then, another half-step.</i>

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.540
<i>He matched the timing 
of my foot moving forward...</i>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.780
<i>As soon as he grabs me, I'll shake him off!</i>

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.500
Kabaddi!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.140
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.430
He can reach all the way over here?

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:49.280
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.930
<i>If he'd caught me, he'd have taken me down.</i>

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.850
<b>Noukin    Souwa</b>

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.100
<i>I won't be taken off guard.</i>

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.850
<i>I'll start by sinking everyone around him.</i>

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.440
<b>Takaya Ren</b>

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.440
<b>Takaya Ren Fan Club</b>

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.440
Ren-kun, two points!

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:53.940
Okay, time for defense!

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.480
Kabaddi.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.430
<i>He chased me?</i>

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.700
You little...!

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.840
<i>You were able to dodge that, huh?</i>

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.710
<i>Bonus!</i>

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.040
He got the bonus point!

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.240
He's coming in hungry!

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.250
We're not letting you get back!

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.500
<i>If we can't read his movement, then...</i>

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.840
<i>we'll block all routes of escape!</i>

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.800
<i>Okay! And I've got the outside covered.</i>

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.840
Kabaddi!

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.270
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.800
<i>He forced an opening?</i>

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.560
<i>Through guys who are stronger than him?</i>

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:24.800
Move, Takaya!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.990
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:29.600
<b>Noukin      Souwa</b>

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.600
<b>Noukin: Ojo, Raid Successful
Bonus 1 pt + Touch 2 pts
3 pts Gained</b>

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.420
What was that just now?

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.540
He was trying to get a touch on Takaya, too!

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.070
He didn't have skills like that before.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.620
Did you think you'd whittle 
away at our defense?

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.010
That won't be possible.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.870
<b>BACK: Misumi, Yoigoshi</b>

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.870
<i>That's scary...</i>

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.620
There were people like this in swimming, too.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.640
People whose personalities and 
movements changed during a match.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.620
I'm feeling nostalgic.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:59.240
I sank all of those guys 
and became number one.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.340
<b>Defense
Noukin 5 Players</b>

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.340
<b>Raid
Souwa / Takaya</b>

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.590
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:07.050
<i>So, he's going after Masato again? But...</i>

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.700
<i>How is he planning to get away?</i>

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.180
<i>I can't read his line of sight.</i>

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.110
Kabaddi!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:17.610
Kabaddi!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:21.360
Kabaddi!

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:24.860
<i>Just one more centimeter.</i>

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.340
Don't go forgetting me!

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.370
Wha?!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.830
This is the good part! Quit interfering!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.010
<i>After that, the two raiders 
fought to take heads.</i>

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.080
<i>They each targeted the other team's ace.</i>

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.970
<b>Noukin     Souwa</b>

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.930
<i>However, the difference between them 
has slowly become apparent.</i>

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.550
They're down to a four-point gap!

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.990
But how? There isn't much difference 
in the number of touches.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.480
<i>The issue is the success rate in bonuses.</i>

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.790
<i>In terms of having a feel for the size of 
the court, Ojo's understanding is superior.</i>

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.990
<i>The amount of sweat they've shed on the 
court is as different as night and day.</i>

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.080
Referee! Time out!

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:10.990
<b>Noukin</b>

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:10.990
<b>Souwa</b>

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.470
Souwa, thirty-second time out!

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.350
Do not give Ojo any more points!

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.870
Our defense will be absolute!

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:18.750
Sir!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.630
What is it, Takaya?

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.140
Nothing. It just seems like they're...

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:25.990
What do you mean?

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:31.850
I am asking you why I can't 
go out on the next raid, Kei.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.440
It's very simple.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.750
They're starting to get used to your movements, 
and they're wearing down your stamina.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.360
The price for coming into the game 
early is demanding to be paid now.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.170
But, in the time we have left...

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:47.820
Yes. By rights, this is when you, 
our ace, should be on the court.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.760
That is, if our ace had the kind 
of strong body that wouldn't break.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:56.560
Raiders are constantly haunted by the 
possibility of a tackle from a blind spot.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.920
Normally, you would be able to dodge, 
or you'd be able to fall safely.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.840
But, not when you're fatigued.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:06.840
The fact that kabaddi is dangerous 
is just how things are.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.890
If you're afraid, you can't win.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.340
Masato.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.480
I'm not telling you to be 
afraid of being injured.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.790
If they break you now, 
that's the end of the tournament, too.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.740
Your dream! Our goals! All of that will end!

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.840
That is what I'm telling you to be afraid of!

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.470
Kei...

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.640
Senpai!

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:31.620
Sorry.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.630
It's fine.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.800
<i>I just...</i>

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.840
Then, why don't you help me win, too?

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.400
It's been six years since 
you scouted me, you know?

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.720
I'm sorry. I understand now. But, I...

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:52.810
You were thinking that you needed to get 
Takaya out on this next raid, right?

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.680
Yeah.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.430
We need to get him out this next turn,

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.140
we'll run out of time and lose.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.380
And Takaya-kun isn't someone an 
average raider can take down.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.020
Yoigoshi-kun.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.030
You're going in my place.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.130
You're the one...

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.900
who can take out Takaya Ren.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.660
<b>Raider
Noukin / Yoigoshi</b>

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.660
<b>Defense
Souwa 5 Players</b>

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:18.490
End of time out!

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:20.660
We will resume with Noukin raiding!

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.670
It's... not Ojo?

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.050
Oh! Here comes Yoigoshi!

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:29.920
I've never seen Yoigoshi 
with that expression before.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.930
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:36.640
Your dream! Our goals! All of that will end!

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.610
You're the one...

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.940
who can take out Takaya Ren.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:46.940
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.150
<i>As long as I win, that's enough.</i>

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.940
<i>That's what I thought, but...</i>

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:50.940
<i>The wildness is gone. Or rather...</i>

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.070
<i>it's more like it's burning inside him.</i>

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:56.650
Kabaddi!

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:00.870
<i>Coming for me, huh? Way too obvious.</i>

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.680
He's transforming.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:03.380
Huh?

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.320
This is probably the first time 
Yoigoshi has experienced this...

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.950
Going out in place of the ace.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.490
A rookie has been entrusted 
with an important role.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.490
For the person with experience, 
there is nothing more frustrating.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.510
Yoigoshi understands that.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.220
That's why, as a rookie,

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:22.120
the only thing he can think 
about is helping the team win.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:26.520
The more desperate you get, the easier 
it is to read your movements.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.570
Why don't we just have some fun with this?

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.440
Shut up.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.910
<i>Sports have always been stupid.</i>

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:39.460
<i>Everyone wracks their brains like idiots,
 practices hard like idiots...</i>

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.940
<i>all so that they can win 
and celebrate like idiots!</i>

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.850
<i>That is why I...</i>

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:50.460
<i>will pull out every last thing 
I've learned from that idiot!</i>

00:08:49.380 --> 00:09:09.490
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.890
<i>He's come pretty deep.</i>

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.420
<i>You think we might be able to get behind him?</i>

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:54.800
<i>Wait.</i>

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.440
<i>He's planning to do a roll kick.</i>

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.300
<i>Be ready to dodge it before you come in.</i>

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.800
<i>His eyes are focused your way.</i>

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.890
<i>That was close!</i>

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.780
<i>He switched his target?</i>

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.240
<i>With a four-point gap, you want 
to score a lot of points, right?</i>

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.460
<i>But if you miss, you'll be wide open.</i>

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.480
<i>Lure him over.</i>

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:17.160
<i>The thing I can do is take
 everything I've done so far and...</i>

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:17.910
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.760
<i>He's coming!</i>

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.570
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:27.820
Wha?!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.870
<i>I'm his target?</i>

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.130
<i>His line of sight was a feint!</i>

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:32.900
<i>I'll stop you!</i>

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.170
<i>I dodged it! I can get back!</i>

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.530
You're not getting back!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.570
<i>He reached out to form a chain?</i>

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.780
Nice, Ei-chan!

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:44.430
Kabaddi!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.850
Rokugen-san, finish him!

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:46.860
Leave it to me!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.760
<i>I always gave it my very best...</i>

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.860
<i>but I lost over and over.</i>

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.360
<i>That's why I...</i>

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:55.670
Kabaddi!

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.040
<i>I will surpass my best!</i>

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.620
<i>Just a little further!</i>

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.170
He got knocked completely into the air!

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:14.630
Kabaddi!

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.060
<i>He's still keeping up the cant?</i>

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.470
<i>I've sunk him so many times.</i>

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:22.970
<i>I've shown him the difference 
in our strength over and over.</i>

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.280
<i>Normally, he should have given up by now.</i>

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.480
<i>But he's...</i>

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.610
<i>What is this burning determination?!</i>

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:32.980
Kabaddi!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.490
Give up! You're already outside the court!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.830
This is how you use long arms and legs.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.290
Hey.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:55.290
As a rookie, I've learned 
quite a lot from you.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:02.130
I made sure to get Takaya out.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:05.340
Let's win this, Senpai.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.300
Yeah.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:11.650
<b>Noukin: Yoigoshi Raid Successful
Touch 2 pts Gained</b>

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.610
Two points to Noukin!

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.650
A t-two-point gap!

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:16.020
That man really is unbelievable.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:18.370
The way he learns...
 His hunger is different!

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:21.150
He's an amateur who's only been 
playing kabaddi for a month, right?

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.670
Surely, even Souwa's carefree 
number three will...

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:28.160
Learned, huh?

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.040
<b>OUT: Takaya, Eikura</b>

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.040
<b>Noukin</b>

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.040
<b>Souwa</b>

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:36.040
<i>Fifty-two seconds remain. 
Souwa has a two-point lead.</i>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.050
<b>Defense
Noukin 5 players</b>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.050
<b>Raider
Souwa / Rokugen</b>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.050
<i>And so, Souwa's raid begins.</i>

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.580
<i>If Rokugen scores even one point, 
Takaya will come back.</i>

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:46.510
<i>For the sake of our final raid, 
we can't let him return.</i>

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.730
<i>There isn't much time. 
We need additional points.</i>

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:52.520
<i>There is still the possibility 
that Ojo will raid.</i>

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:56.480
<i>I must touch at least two people and 
return our defense to five players!</i>

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:58.440
Kabaddi.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.690
This tension is insane.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.040
The chances left are few,

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.990
but they do exist and his will 
to make good on them is strong.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.580
Who will he target?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.000
Kabaddi.

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:14.480
<i>Ojo's legs still have life in them.</i>

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:18.210
<i>In that case, Noukin's last raider, 
thinking in terms of attack power,</i>

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.700
<i>will be one of those two.</i>

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.520
<i>That means that those two are unlikely 
to risk coming in for a catch!</i>

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.950
<i>I will smack down any half-hearted tackles.</i>

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:29.100
<i>If they lose their nerve and fall back, 
I will take the bonus!</i>

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:31.100
<i>What will you do, Noukin?</i>

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.290
<i>He's way too focused on the captain!</i>

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:37.210
<i>Will you come to capture me,
 you frail raider?</i>

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.370
<i>He's not showing any sign of running...</i>

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:40.360
That jerk!

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:41.890
Kabaddi.

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.410
<i>He's choosing who he's dodging!</i>

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.150
<i>We need to take him down fast!</i>

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:47.370
Don't panic!

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:51.070
<i>Even if we only have one second left,
 once we start raiding,</i>

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:53.310
<i>the game continues until our raid is over.</i>

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:56.200
Don't let Rokugen score! That's all 
you need to think about right now!

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:57.210
Kabaddi.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:58.710
<i>Here he comes.</i>

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.190
<i>Hey.</i>

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:06.580
<i>I wasn't even looking at you.</i>

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.310
<i>You're not worried about me at all?</i>

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.730
<i>Rokugen, you were the same 
the first time we met.</i>

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:16.800
Starting today, I'll be joining 
the selection practices.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.490
I'm Rokugen Ayumu. I'm looking 
forward to training with you.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:24.150
He's a middle school first-year
 and just started kabaddi this spring.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.860
For now, we'll have him mix 
in with the second string.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:30.440
<i>I was the one with more 
experience in kabaddi.</i>

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:34.160
<i>A big guy had started playing on a whim...</i>

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:35.960
<i>That's what I thought.</i>

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.560
<i>And the truth was he knew 
next to nothing about kabaddi.</i>

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:52.700
Kabaddi! Kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.670
What's a "raid failed" decision?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:46.510
It's when a referee determines that it's 
impossible for the raider to return.

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:50.100
The word "struggle" originally meant 
just that, a struggle to get back.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:54.020
Even if you're caught, as long as you 
keep fighting to get back to home ground,

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.580
the raid isn't over.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:14:00.410
<i>There was a reason Rokugen didn't have 
a deep understanding of the rules.</i>

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.520
<i>Up until that point, as soon as the 
opponent got caught, it was over.</i>

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.640
<i>He had never allowed anyone 
to struggle to get back.</i>

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:12.330
<i>That was the last day Rokugen 
practiced with the second string.</i>

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.330
Those guys on the first string
 really are on a different level.

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.770
<i>There's such a clear, visible 
difference between us...</i>

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.920
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.240
Kabaddi!

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.960
<i>As I thought, Ojo isn't 
coming in to catch me!</i>

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:30.440
That's our raider!

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.800
Don't touch him!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.390
<i>The antis' containment maneuvers are good.</i>

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.450
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.850
<i>At the winter tournament, they felt like a 
one-man team with a bunch of helpers.</i>

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.440
<i>I see you've helped them grow, Ojo!</i>

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.860
<i>It wasn't me, Rokugen.</i>

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:47.980
<i>The one who helped our team grow wasn't me.</i>

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:53.490
<b>Noukin</b>

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:53.490
<b>Souwa</b>

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:51.630
<i>It's already been more than thirty 
seconds since he started his cant!</i>

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:52.970
<i>The next touch...</i>

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:54.600
<i>will be his real aim!</i>

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:57.750
Kabaddi!

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:01.450
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:03.770
<i>What?!</i>

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.500
<i>He wasn't aiming for the raiders?</i>

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.510
Two of them got touched!

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:12.150
<i>If I targeted the raiders, I knew 
it would draw in the defense!</i>

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:15.360
<i>If I get two points here, 
then even if Ojo raids next,</i>

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:18.100
<i>we'll be able to push him back, 
though we'll pay a price for it.</i>

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>Those two will not be able to catch up to me!</i>

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.000
We can catch up to you.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.900
We will stop you!

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.270
<i>Wh-Why are the raiders...</i>

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:35.330
<i>I thought that, for the sake of the
 last raid, they would avoid risk!</i>

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.900
Kabaddi...

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.350
<i>If I don't persevere now, 
how can I call myself captain?</i>

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:46.960
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.700
<i>I am finished with my selfishness.</i>

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:47.290
<i>I will return... to my teammates!</i>

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:51.320
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:52.550
It's useless! It's exactly like the plan. 
We can't stop him!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.970
Iura!

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:55.610
<i>All the raiders?</i>

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:00.120
<i>I've thought it over for years...</i>

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.270
<i>How can I catch up to him?</i>

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.730
<i>The methods I arrived at were 
to analyze the enemy's thinking,</i>

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.610
<i>and to take action in unexpected ways.</i>

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:10.970
<i>The only thing that can make up 
for a difference in ability...</i>

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:13.850
<i>is strategy!</i>

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.910
We'll finish him!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:18.910
Kabaddi...

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.300
<i>I will return...</i>

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:23.770
<i>As long as my heart... As long 
as my heart doesn't waver!</i>

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:27.010
<i>As long as the struggle continues, 
the raid isn't over!</i>

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.190
<i>My arm!</i>

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:35.500
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:34.260
<i>How far ahead has this man read?</i>

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.890
<i>Let go!</i>

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:40.320
<i>I'm giving everything I've got 
against just one of your arms.</i>

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.060
<i>It hardly seems worth it, right?</i>

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.660
<i>This is cruel.</i>

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:47.130
<i>In the end, I feel keenly the 
difference in our abilities.</i>

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:51.280
<i>Still, the reason I can keep fighting...</i>

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:57.880
<i>It must be because, 
despite all the painful things,</i>

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:01.000
<i>the fun of kabaddi outweighs them, right?</i>

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:03.310
Iura!

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:04.020
Kei!

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.180
Iura-san!

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:09.170
Kabaddi... Kabaddi...

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:09.170
<i>I can't hear anything...</i>

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:12.080
<i>"Ojo's friend."</i>

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:20.520
Kabaddi... Kabaddi...

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:16.680
<i>I'll ask him myself. I must ask him.</i>

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:21.370
<i>I must ask the name of the powerful 
opponent who defeated me.</i>

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:25.160
Th-They stopped him.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:26.840
The raid.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:27.770
Let's go!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:33.520
<b>Noukin</b>

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:33.520
<b>Souwa</b>

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:30.580
Souwa, raid failed!

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:32.310
One point to Noukin!

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:33.530
And time is up!

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:35.540
End of match!

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:39.530
The game... is over?

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.540
Yeah! Yay! All right!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.220
We had fifty seconds left!

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:46.040
There's no way his cant 
could have lasted that long!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:50.040
Stop, Yoigoshi-kun. 
A fifty-second cant isn't impossible.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.270
It was a mistake on our part.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.420
<i>No matter how strong the opponent, 
they cannot beat time.</i>

00:17:55.950 --> 00:18:00.410
<i>Noukin, you timed the Souwa lona for 
the end of the first half, didn't you?</i>

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:04.390
<i>I employed your use of time as a reference.</i>

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:09.350
This is where it was supposed to start. 
We'd defeated Takaya and Rokugen.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.650
When is it?

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.490
Huh?

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:13.950
When is the tournament?

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:15.860
Yoigoshi-kun...

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:21.270
Take a good look.

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:25.370
The strong, and those who will become 
strong, their hearts are different.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:29.580
They keep anger and conflict deep inside, 
and keep their eyes focused ahead.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:34.100
It isn't easy, but they know that if 
they don't, they won't be able to win.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.490
They continue to suffer until 
they stand at the summit,

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.660
like people who have been cursed.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.790
The tournament is in August.

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:45.640
August... Three months from now, then.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:49.600
For us third-years, it's our last tournament.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.650
We can't afford to lose. 
We must claw our way up.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:57.220
With a score of 32 to 31, Souwa wins! Bow!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:59.110
Thank you for the game!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.330
Aren't you offering your 
handshake to the wrong person?

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.850
This is no mistake.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:13.350
My formidable opponent, 
I did not know you had such strength.

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.590
Please, tell me your name!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.720
<i>The fact he doesn't have any 
ill-intent is infuriating.</i>

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:22.510
I'm "Ojo's friend." 
Make sure you remember it.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.740
Huh? That's not a name, is it?

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:28.470
My name is Iura Kei. Nice to meet you.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.820
What do you think you're doing?!

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:30.800
Iura, is it?

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.160
Iura Kei is shy.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:35.600
Getting all chummy with the enemy.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.400
Takaya...

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:42.410
Don't make such a scary face. Here.

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:43.960
There's no need.

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:44.910
Really?

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.910
You're a cocky one, aren't you?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.080
Do you want to beat me?

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:50.930
Of course I do!

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.670
What'll you do if you beat me?

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.910
Some other strong opponent 
will probably show up.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:56.940
You'll beat him, and it'll just repeat.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.470
I'll think about that 
after I become number one!

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:03.970
Then come and chase me with 
everything you've got.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.240
I've got someone I'm chasing, too.

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:09.110
Here's hoping this isn't the 
last time you get touched by me.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:11.100
So you've got no intention of 
catching me when you're on defense?

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:13.680
You say some dumb things, Rookie-kun.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.940
It's not "Rookie-kun." 
The name's Yoigoshi Tatsuya.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:20.610
You should at least remember the 
name of the next person to beat you!

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.510
Well, you're free to say 
whatever you want, right?

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:24.660
Tattsun.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.370
Cut it out! That makes it 
sound like I'm a little kid!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:30.120
<b>Takaya Ren</b>

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.610
That's fine, isn't it?

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:28.900
It is not fine!

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.120
Tattsun!

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.170
<i>Takaya scored 27 points.</i>

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.070
<i>The captain scored 23 points.</i>

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:40.540
<i>I only scored seven points.</i>

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:43.640
<i>On days I lose, I never 
feel like I can sleep.</i>

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:47.190
<i>Saying that the weak tried their 
hardest is just pretty words.</i>

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:48.670
<i>A loss is a loss.</i>

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:50.600
<i>If this were a tournament, 
it would be the end!</i>

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:51.830
Damn it!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.440
What are you doing?

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:07.000
I practiced a ton, 
but I couldn't do anything.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:12.550
When our team was catching up, 
when you were accomplishing so much,

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.250
I just couldn't be fully happy.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.750
Are you stupid?

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:20.960
Not being able to execute what you 
practiced during a real match is common.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.630
You might be able to use a 
third of your strength. Or not.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:27.710
Since you don't know any other sports, your 
awareness in this area is undeveloped.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:32.250
Losing just means the other guys did more.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.940
You really are amazing...

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.380
Of course I am.

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.110
I was once a child prodigy, 
a genius, unstoppable...

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.820
an elite called by many different names.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.720
Why is a person like me playing kabaddi?

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:47.900
Why?

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:52.680
Who do you think the first person 
to stop the "Unstoppable" was?

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:01.890
If you lose, you bring my name down, too.

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:04.590
If you have time to be depressed, 
then you should practice.

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:08.990
I really am glad I started kabaddi.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:14.600
Starting now... 
Azemichi Soma won't lose anymore!

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.810
Come on, let's run, Yoigoshi!

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.180
You little...

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:24.360
I-It wasn't on purpose!

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:25.500
You fall in, too!

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:30.760
<i>In the new team's first practice 
match, a match against Souwa,</i>

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:32.490
<i>they lost by one point.</i>

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:38.450
<i>But, little by little... 
they are moving forward.</i>

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"Team Applicants"</b>

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:52.410
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:52.410
Next time, "Team Applicants!"

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:53.320
Kabaddi!
